    "created_at": "2019-10-28T09:04:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-28T09:04:40Z",
    "body": "In Validator.nu/Firefox, there's a flag `needToDropLF` on the tree builder. It is\r\n\r\n* Set to `false` at the start of the parse.\r\n* Set to `false` at the beginning of processing a non-character token.\r\n* Set to `true` when processing a `textarea`, `pre`, or `listing` start tag token. (Happens after the previous bullet point.)\r\n* Set to `false` after the tree builder has processed the generated `pre` start tag for `text/plain`. (After the previous bullet point.)\r\n* Checked (and then always set to `false`) at the start of processing of character tokens (if the incoming character token is LF and the flag was `true`, the LF is dropped).\r\n\r\nI believe the spec should have this kind of flag.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
